1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,795
Regulation Crowdfunding, often
called Reg CF, is a U.S.

2
00:00:03,795 --> 00:00:07,887
securities exemption that lets
eligible companies raise money

3
00:00:07,887 --> 00:00:09,429
from the public online.

4
00:00:09,429 --> 00:00:13,116
An offering must be conducted
through an SEC-registered

5
00:00:13,116 --> 00:00:15,262
broker-dealer or funding portal.

6
00:00:15,262 --> 00:00:17,544
It is not simply a company posting

7
00:00:17,544 --> 00:00:20,498
a payment link and calling it an
investment.

8
00:00:20,498 --> 00:00:24,711
The company files disclosures,
usually on Form C, and investors

9
00:00:24,711 --> 00:00:27,921
review those documents through
the intermediary.

10
00:00:27,921 --> 00:00:31,961
Non-accredited investors are
subject to aggregate investment

11
00:00:31,961 --> 00:00:33,980
limits across Reg CF offerings

12
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:36,471
during a rolling twelve-month
period.

13
00:00:36,471 --> 00:00:40,349
The company may raise up to five
million dollars under the

14
00:00:40,349 --> 00:00:44,160
exemption in a twelve-month
period, subject to the rules.

15
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:48,041
Securities bought in a Reg CF
offering generally cannot be

16
00:00:48,041 --> 00:00:51,053
resold for one year, with limited
exceptions.

17
00:00:51,053 --> 00:00:54,807
The SEC filing is not an
endorsement of the company or a

18
00:00:54,807 --> 00:00:56,952
prediction that it will succeed.

19
00:00:56,952 --> 00:01:01,495
Read the offering carefully, verify
the intermediary, and understand

20
00:01:01,495 --> 00:01:05,369
that startup losses and long
holding periods are possible.

21
00:01:05,369 --> 00:01:09,960
These rules describe Reg CF, not
every kind of startup fundraising.

